WEBVTT

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.740
<i>The UN Security Council demanded that</i>

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:20.520
<i>the Japanese government turn over 
the Wam, a source of infinite energy.</i>

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.450
<b>Hand over the Wam now!</b>

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.450
<b>Inuzuka should
resign!</b>

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:24.250
<i>Yaha-kui zaShunina and Shindo Kojiro decided</i>

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:29.140
<i>to solve this problem by requesting 
the help of Shinawa Kanata.</i>

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.550
<i>After his conversation 
with Yaha-kui zaShunina,</i>

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:36.310
<i>Prime Minister Inuzuka Kozo decided to</i>

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:42.060
<i>share the method to create Wam that 
Dr. Shinawa invented with the entire world.</i>

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:48.550
<i>It was the decision of a politician who 
knew it could cause pain for humanity.</i>

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.160
Tetrok

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:55.300
There.

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:02.320
<b>Mifune Lab</b>

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:04.570
Only two people besides you 
have been able to make them.

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:08.450
They were only successful once, 
and haven't been able to reproduce it.

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:12.710
No, no, Doctor, anyone can do it.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:15.440
I mean, maybe it takes a little practice...

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:18.570
Your idea of "a little" doesn't 
apply to anyone else.

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:24.100
Well, because it's so hard to make, 
the world's avoided falling into chaos.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:21.700
<b>What the Anisotropic Wants</b>

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.850
<b>New Energy Source, Wam
Less Than 0.1% Successful Creation Rate 
Unknown Factor Involved?</b>

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:25.610
But, but...

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:29.360
It seemed like he understood 
perfectly, even better than me.

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:37.290
You understand well the 
essential nature of the Wam.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.550
Hey, zaShunina,

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:42.320
why am I able to make these?

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:46.870
A sense of the anisotropic is 
required to create the Wam.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.990
So not just anyone can make it?

00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:50.960
Anyone can.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:54.120
However, some are better than others.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.630
The more one's brain is 
optimized for this universe,

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:59.630
the less it is able to 
adapt to the anisotropic.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:03.730
It's difficult for the elderly to understand 
the anisotropic structure of the Wam.

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:05.890
It's easier for children to accept it.

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:08.740
Shinawa Kanata is an adult,

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:11.100
but her mental structure 
is that of a child's.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:15.780
That's why she was able to learn 
how to make the Wam so easily.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:18.440
That's quite a mean thing to say.

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:22.610
Does that mean I have 
the brain of a child, too?

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:25.060
Your ability is due to special circumstances.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:28.620
You underwent Kado's processing.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:32.660
Then the passengers who were released

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:37.380
were forcibly given a sense of 
the anisotropic when they left?

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.090
No.

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:41.920
It's just you, Shindo.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:46.600
You were the first human 
to undergo the processing.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:50.210
At that point, the available 
information was still inadequate.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.980
So the processing failed?

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:56.310
I would like you to think of 
it as excessively successful.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:58.960
You are a premium human

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:02.320
who took in far more of 
a sense of the anisotropic.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:05.430
To me, this was a joyous event.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:10.750
You are the factor that's functioning 
extremely well as a bridge between

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:12.830
humanity and the anisotropic.

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:16.500
I would like you to continue to do this.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:20.250
If you're too selfish, 
you won't make any friends.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:21.580
"Friends."

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:24.300
A vague concept, isn't it?

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:29.740
Anisotropic being, Yaha-kui zaShunina,

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:32.550
if you want to improve relations 
between humanity and the anisotropic,

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:35.820
there are many problems that must be solved.

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:40.770
<b>Presently Released: 72/251 People</b>

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:40.090
The release of the passengers is going well.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.350
So, next is...

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:45.610
This.

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:48.570
Moving Kado From Its Present Position

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:48.570
What about above the sea?

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:49.710
Unsuitable.

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:52.580
Kado does not possess 
the concept of "floating,"

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:58.170
but it's better to have a certain amount of
contact surface with minimal amplitude.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:00.640
It can't get smaller?

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:01.940
That is less than ideal.

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:04.020
This location is optimal.

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:08.180
By location, do you mean 
three-dimensional coordinates?

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:10.480
21%.

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:14.080
My understanding of dimensions 
is different from yours.

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:16.940
A shared understanding of the 
concept of "location" is difficult.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.820
But it does have to stay
two kilometers to a side?

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:26.060
Then you'll have to get 
pretty far out of Tokyo...

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:27.690
That is less than ideal, as well.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:31.420
The reason is your mental states.

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:35.950
Let us hypothesize that Kado moved here.

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:39.510
The introduction of factors 
besides the Japanese nation

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:42.780
will cause a severe drop in the 
speed of information exchange.

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:44.040
I see.

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:47.760
What zaShunina is referring 
to isn't physical location.

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:53.080
He doesn't want to be located too 
far from the Japanese government.

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:56.940
But finding two square kilometers of 
level ground in eastern Japan...

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:58.460
It does not need to be level.

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:02.000
So long as the ground is stable, 
with amplitude below a certain level,

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:04.620
Kado can alter its shape 
to make contact with it.

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:09.190
Sayama Lake

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:09.190
How about here?

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:13.920
Sayama Lake?

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:20.500
<i>The Japanese government just announced 
that the anisotropic has agreed to move</i>

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:19.910
<b><i>Breaking News</i></b>

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:19.910
<b>Potential New Kado Location Decided</b>

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:22.290
Local Response Team Forward Base
for Large Cube That Appeared on 7/25

00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:24.310
<b>August 8th</b>

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:22.640
<i>the massive object at Haneda airport,</i>

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:25.250
<i>known as "Kado."</i>

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:28.380
<i>They have also said that 
the current candidate</i>

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:30.840
<b><i>Breaking News</i></b>

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:30.840
<b>Potential New Kado Location Decided</b>

00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:31.620
<i>for a new location is the 
area around Sayama Lake.</i>

00:07:29.030 --> 00:07:30.840
Saitama: Sayama Lake

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:32.820
Of course I'm following them!

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:36.520
<i>They have already begun negotiations 
with the local governments.</i>

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:36.390
Here we go, huh?

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:39.690
Yup. It's moving somewhere 
close to the capital, too.

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:42.290
<i>The area selected includes the cities of 
Tokorozawa, Iruma, Musashimurayama, and...</i>

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:42.290
There's gonna be tons of 
complaints and protests.

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:45.060
Gonno-san, there's a press conference!

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:45.640
<i>The appearance of the anisotropic is</i>

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:48.900
the most important event 
in our country's history.

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:53.710
I ask all citizens for their 
understanding and cooperation

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:56.860
in overcoming this emergency.

00:07:56.860 --> 00:08:00.460
Ubuka-san's planning to use the emergency 
laws to force his way through this.

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:01.500
Which means...

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:03.730
The move isn't far off.

00:08:04.260 --> 00:08:06.080
The most likely day is...

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:10.630
August 26th.

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:14.300
All passengers trapped inside Kado

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:16.220
will be released by the 25th.

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:18.480
The move will be performed the next day.

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:23.730
We've picked a location that minimizes effects 
on the populace and surrounding facilities...

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:26.150
<b>Iruma</b>

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:26.150
<b>Zuiho</b>

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:26.150
<b>Hamura</b>

00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:26.150
Here.

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:29.610
The next question is how, exactly, it moves.

00:08:30.970 --> 00:08:34.050
Can you do the same thing 
you did when it appeared?

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:36.680
In other words, disappear,

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:39.350
then reappear at the location?

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:44.420
When manifesting in this 
universe from the anisotropic,

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:47.770
I did precise tuning across 
multiple dimensions.

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:50.960
I would like to avoid leaving and returning.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:53.790
Also, if it's going to move directly,

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:57.950
it would be best if contact was kept 
with a fixed surface along the ground.

00:08:58.810 --> 00:08:59.750
In other words...

00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:00.970
This.

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:12.220
You're going to roll it?

00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:17.240
What happens to whatever's below it?

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:22.740
If I devote my full energy to controlling Kado, 
I can avoid absorbing whatever is below it,

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:24.140
as well as destroying it.

00:09:24.550 --> 00:09:26.080
And if that is something living?

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:27.800
It will not be destroyed,

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:31.590
but there may be a minor effect on its mind.

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:34.910
So a temporary evacuation is unavoidable.

00:09:34.910 --> 00:09:39.330
Is there any way to minimize 
the contact surface?

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:47.530
zaShunina, is this possible?

00:09:54.590 --> 00:09:55.740
It is.

00:09:58.640 --> 00:09:59.750
Asano.

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:00.950
Got it.

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:03.930
We'll use that idea to come 
up with a plan for the move.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:08.520
<b>Transportation Section</b>

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:09.980
<b>August 12th</b>

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:21.260
<b>Notice of Transportation Restrictions</b>

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:23.120
<b>August 17th</b>

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:25.080
Wide-Area Notice
August 26: While Kado Moves,
Large-Scale Transportation Restrictions
 Will Be In Effect

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:27.680
<b>August 20th</b>

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:31.170
<b>Notice of Temporary Evacuation</b>

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:31.170
Please Comply as Kado Moves

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:36.740
<b>August 21st</b>

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:46.420
You're not going to rest?

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:48.540
Thanks.

00:10:57.600 --> 00:10:58.380
It's good.

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:02.300
I don't think I'm pushing myself too hard,

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:05.170
but it's strange how much I've 
been capable of working lately.

00:11:05.710 --> 00:11:08.600
A negotiator has a duty 
to take regular breaks.

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:11.770
I know that, but...

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:14.060
How long has it been since you had a break?

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:15.750
Um...

00:11:25.880 --> 00:11:26.830
Shindo-san!

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:29.840
Take tomorrow off, please!

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:31.670
I don't know...

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:34.350
I wouldn't really have anything to do...

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:57.480
What are you supposed to be? 
Some kind of movie star?

00:11:57.890 --> 00:12:00.410
I'm famous lately, you see.

00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:03.860
I'm back.

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:06.630
Welcome back, Kojiro.

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:19.050
Who eats grilled squid tentacles for lunch?

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:20.890
It's all I've got.

00:12:23.780 --> 00:12:25.000
You're off today, right?

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:27.140
I am.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:28.720
Then it's okay, right?

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:43.950
Oh, they say that big thing's 
coming through here.

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:43.950
<b>Notice of Temporary Evacuation</b>

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:43.950
Please Comply as Kado Moves

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:46.540
Will everything be okay?

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:47.970
It will.

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:51.500
But just to be safe, I want you 
to evacuate temporarily.

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:57.620
Oh, did you come because you were worried?

00:12:57.620 --> 00:13:00.630
I'd feel bad if I never got to see you again.

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:02.510
Don't even say that.

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:10.100
So what's the deal with that alien?

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:12.020
The "anisotropic being."

00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:14.020
I don't know...

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:15.770
He's still full of mysteries.

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:17.920
He's not human, right?

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:19.060
That's right.

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:21.530
His fundamental concepts 
are different from ours,

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:25.970
so even if we speak the same language, a lot 
of stuff doesn't completely get through.

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:27.320
Sounds tough.

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:33.180
Does this "anisotropic being" have parents?

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:36.190
Can it have children, I wonder?

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:38.630
I don't know.

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:41.580
The breeding method of 
the anisotropic beings...

00:13:41.580 --> 00:13:45.500
No, its current form is 
likely a temporary one.

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:48.410
We don't even know what it really looks like.

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:51.230
Why?

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:55.090
Well, it would be lonely if 
it was all by itself, right?

00:13:55.090 --> 00:13:58.310
It's fun to drink with 
your children, you know.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:01.110
That's how it is, huh?

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:04.340
That's right.

00:14:10.220 --> 00:14:13.450
<b>August 25th</b>

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:15.200
<b>Presently Released: 250/251 People</b>

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:38.350
I'm finally... I'm finally out, Shindo-san!

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:41.730
You hung in there a long time, Hanamori.

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:43.630
Shindo-san!

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:48.070
<b>Kado Movement Project
Moving Day Process List</b>

00:14:47.290 --> 00:14:48.070
What's this?

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:51.360
Work starts at 6:00 AM tomorrow.

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:59.210
<b>August 26th</b>

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:05.120
Section 1 complete.

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:06.430
Section 2 complete.

00:15:06.430 --> 00:15:07.710
Section 3 complete.

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:09.280
This is Haneda start point.

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:10.380
Roger.

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:14.190
Shindo, sections 1 through 3 are evacuated.

00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:15.850
They're ready to go.

00:15:17.050 --> 00:15:18.590
How are we defending the car?

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:25.320
A barrier that tank rounds 
can't penetrate, huh?

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:28.400
Nothing could make me feel safer.

00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:34.240
Kado, begin movement!

00:15:48.020 --> 00:15:49.090
Kado.

00:16:06.810 --> 00:16:09.820
This is the outside of the 
rolling Kado restriction zone.

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:11.340
It's 6:00 AM.

00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:14.230
It seems like Kado's started 
moving right on time!

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:38.970
Section 1, shift position.

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:42.010
Section 1, shift position.

00:16:42.010 --> 00:16:42.980
Kado.

00:17:09.500 --> 00:17:12.300
Angle of contact, 18 degrees!

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:13.760
16!

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:15.700
14!

00:17:16.630 --> 00:17:18.180
12!

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:19.560
10!

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:21.390
8!

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:23.270
6!

00:17:23.630 --> 00:17:24.710
4!

00:17:25.340 --> 00:17:26.510
2!

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:27.360
1!

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:28.560
Contact!

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:36.780
Section 1, contact confirmed.

00:17:37.680 --> 00:17:38.800
Roger.

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:39.990
Section 1 complete.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:43.640
Now prepare to move to section 2.

00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:44.610
<i>Roger.</i>

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:49.960
<b>View of the City</b>

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:49.960
<b><i>Breaking News</i></b>

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:49.960
<b>Kado Begins to Move 
Final Destination is Sayama Lake</b>

00:17:46.510 --> 00:17:49.960
<i>We'll continue to bring you the 
latest news on Kado's movements.</i>

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:56.860
<i>Kado is presently moving from 
section 8 to section 9.</i>

00:17:57.550 --> 00:18:03.400
<i>Those who live in sections 14 and 
15, it is now time to evacuate.</i>

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:08.440
<i>Please obey police instructions and move 
to the temporary evacuation shelters.</i>

00:18:15.850 --> 00:18:17.590
It's huge!

00:18:17.590 --> 00:18:19.450
Is that for real?

00:18:20.440 --> 00:18:22.160
What's going on?

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:24.720
I suppose you could call it a Kado jam.

00:18:25.300 --> 00:18:27.160
Do something, Emi!

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:28.290
Don't ask for the impossible.

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:29.540
Oh, just do it!

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:29.540
Hey, Gonno-san!

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:31.270
That's dangerous!

00:18:29.930 --> 00:18:31.270
Just floor the accelerator!

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:32.370
Gonno-san!

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:36.640
4, 2, 1, contact!

00:18:39.400 --> 00:18:41.970
Section 19, contact confirmed.

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:43.040
Roger.

00:18:43.460 --> 00:18:45.180
Moving to section 20.

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:08.490
Hurry! Get to work!

00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:09.710
Right!

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:13.460
Sayama final point.

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:14.590
Begin contact.

00:19:15.290 --> 00:19:16.470
Sayama final point.

00:19:16.470 --> 00:19:17.560
Begin contact.

00:19:18.250 --> 00:19:19.300
Kado.

00:19:57.840 --> 00:19:59.420
Sayama final point.

00:19:59.420 --> 00:20:00.670
Contact confirmed.

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:03.120
<i>Kado's move is complete!</i>

00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:09.680
Kado's move is complete.

00:20:23.020 --> 00:20:24.070
Shindo.

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:31.370
I want to express my gratitude for 
your negotiations in this matter.

00:20:33.640 --> 00:20:35.270
You're welcome.

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:40.510
A new local HQ will be set 
up below here tomorrow.

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:44.190
The one at Haneda was more 
of a temporary affair,

00:20:44.190 --> 00:20:47.780
but this one will be enough to 
last for the medium to long term.

00:20:48.990 --> 00:20:52.520
There aren't many who can make Wam yet,

00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:54.790
but more will appear.

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:57.150
A real revolution will come.

00:20:58.510 --> 00:21:00.410
Before that happens, I want to exchange

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:03.170
as much information as 
possible with the anisotropic.

00:21:05.560 --> 00:21:06.390
Shindo.

00:21:08.290 --> 00:21:09.330
Next.

00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:11.540
Next?

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:14.120
Energy is the basis of 
the phenomenon of life.

00:21:14.430 --> 00:21:16.760
Providing enough was the first problem.

00:21:17.860 --> 00:21:22.130
Humanity, thanks to the Wam,
now has more energy that it needs.

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:25.020
There's no need to worry about it further.

00:21:26.170 --> 00:21:28.920
Now humanity can take the next step.

00:21:30.160 --> 00:21:30.960
Shindo.

00:21:33.410 --> 00:21:35.270
How long has it been since you slept?

00:21:55.550 --> 00:21:57.140
Humanity will no longer

00:22:01.170 --> 00:22:02.630
need to sleep.

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:38.810
July 25th, 2017.

00:23:38.810 --> 00:23:40.730
That's when it came.

00:23:40.730 --> 00:23:44.270
Yaha-kui zaShunina, why did 
you come to this universe?

00:23:44.270 --> 00:23:47.190
Tell me your honest opinion 
about the anisotropic being.

00:23:47.190 --> 00:23:50.150
Shindo, I am moving on to the next.

00:23:48.550 --> 00:23:52.000
Ekwari
